[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports describe
three problems. The queued parser fix closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Two of the three problems have no ticket and no fix. Each now has its own ticket, linked below.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/DevinEdwards/mega-dev-S01E03-devin/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/DevinEdwards/mega-dev-S01E03-devin/issues/2',
    shift: 'https://github.com/DevinEdwards/mega-dev-S01E03-devin/issues/3',
  }}
  labels={{
    parser: 'shared parser reads day-first dates month first',
    hint: 'booking-v3 form hint says MM/DD, the form reads DD/MM',
    shift: 'invite one day off, not a day/month swap',
  }}
/>

## How to tell them apart

- **parser:** day and month swap places (7 April becomes 4 July). Any day-first tenant, any
  channel except the booking-v3 form.
- **hint:** the same swap, but it comes in through the form of a booking-v3 tenant. The form
  prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, people type month first, and the form reads it day
  first. Fixing the parser does not change the hint.
- **shift:** the date moves by one day, or differs by the reader's time zone ("Client in Lisbon
  got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."). A day/month swap cannot do that. The desk had
  already listed these five in `desk-notes.json` and filed them under parser.

The table counts each report once. The export repeats some reports across pages; they are
dropped by id.

## Why they ended up in one ticket

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. "Date is wrong"
and four other subjects turn up in all three problems, so all three landed in #4471. The
explorer on [triage](/kb/triage/dedupe) already shows each report's cause; check it before
merging into a known ticket.

